{"title":"Quadratic equation","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>quadratic equation</b> in one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Variable\" title=\"Variable\">variable</a> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/7854463d4f6c501eac3c68f01afca574dd1ca73f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a}{x}^2+{b}{x}+{c}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a461ee4b9981db5fb0e010aae769431be4d3cc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constants</a> (that is, they do not depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the unknown variable.  Quadratic equations are solved using one of three main strategies: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring\" title=\"Factoring\">factoring</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">completing the square</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Forms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Forms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Factoring\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Factoring</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Opening\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Opening</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Width\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Width</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Axis_of_symmetry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Axis of symmetry</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Vertex\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Vertex</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Increasing/Decreasing_Intervals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Increasing/Decreasing Intervals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Completing_the_square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Completing the square</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Quadratic_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quadratic Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Forms\">Forms</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Forms\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <b>standard form</b> of a quadratic equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/28969a57466b0a1047fca37478da706c1cb8cced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" />.</li>\n<li>The <b>factored form</b> of a quadratic equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/7576ad4aa2ffa1145f06faf5d12664ceeba43613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=(x-r)(x-s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roots\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Roots\">roots</a> of the function.</li>\n<li>The <b>vertex form</b> of a quadratic equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab0d4716cfb38748ebcbb928280c024e963d993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=a(x-h)^2+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the <b>vertex</b> (see below) of the function.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Factoring\">Factoring</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Factoring\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The purpose of factoring is to turn a general quadratic into a product of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial\" title=\"Binomial\">binomials</a>. This is easier to illustrate than to describe.\n</p><p>Example: Solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d51dced775e273dc9699181601dd8b18b78545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-3x+2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Note: This is different for all quadratics; we cleverly chose this so that it has common factors.\n</p><p>Solution: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d51dced775e273dc9699181601dd8b18b78545c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-3x+2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>First, we expand the middle term: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f680cb335d6d0ff36c7ef4bc8c17de4d00f31dc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-x-2x+2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we factor out our common terms to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11cb8b3edaaafcfae30c4c8065daaf4eba7dd6fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-1)-2(x-1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can now factor the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> term to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/903719e118778a59337eda2f412e50160c6acd81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)(x-2)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. By the zero-product property, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04854d8381ed4ccf9eff2a54ea58b2059b8a454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> equals zero. \n</p><p>We now have the pair of equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307014a15ea78fa9fe437fac446749f7a1e095af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98c65ea9f55940f86f4fd9365e6fd39ad8008a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-2=0$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />. These give us the answers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, which can also be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2736449aeb962d350d06209490ba468740d8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\{1,\\,2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging these back into the original equation, we find that both of these work! We are done.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A quadratic function's properties all depend on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (their coeffiecients):\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Opening\">Opening</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Opening\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, the graph opens up and vice versa.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Width\">Width</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Width\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The smaller <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1967b56d9ecac019dd3a05ac931053bf2442d146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|{a}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" /> is, the wider (or fatter, as some people would say) the graph gets.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Axis_of_symmetry\">Axis of symmetry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Axis of symmetry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The axis of symmetry of a quadratic function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121cd605cf7dc1e301ccc7c17f9ad3cb39ca2c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Vertex\">Vertex</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Vertex\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The vertex of a function is the point where the tone of the function changes. It is also the maximum or minimum value of a function. The vertex formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd444a84a35393f764aeaa0034a9772dda834af6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\frac{b}{2a},\\frac{b^2-4ac}{4a})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Increasing.2FDecreasing_Intervals\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Increasing/Decreasing_Intervals\">Increasing/Decreasing Intervals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Increasing/Decreasing Intervals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>For when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> the increasing interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792c9928f290ac6cde18c808e001ac159872d7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" /> and the decreasing interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf380adc0cafa40c2d01204baf9e397a5ea1b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" />.</li>\n<li>For when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8362e1f78725beb1de44c30360f0a10d0d3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> the increasing interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf380adc0cafa40c2d01204baf9e397a5ea1b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" /> and the decreasing interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792c9928f290ac6cde18c808e001ac159872d7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" />.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Completing_the_square\">Completing the square</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Completing the square\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">Completing the square </a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quadratic_Formula\">Quadratic Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Quadratic Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_Formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quadratic Formula\">Quadratic Formula</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">Discriminant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_Inequality\" title=\"Quadratic Inequality\">Quadratic Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factoring_Quadratics\" title=\"Factoring Quadratics\">Factoring Quadratics</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017120236\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 233/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6777/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1651:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017120236 and revision id 277960. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}